{
  "id": "COMPOUND:44353 - DISEASE:829",
  "verbalization": "The compound [(1R,2R,3R,4S,7R,9S,10S,11R,12R,15S)-2,9,11,12-tetraacetyloxy-4-hydroxy-10,14,17,17-tetramethyl-6-oxatetracyclo[11.3.1.03,10.04,7]heptadec-13-en-15-yl] acetate is associated with Diabetic Angiopathies through multiple pathways. It is observed to affect the FGF signaling regulator 3, which in turn causes Genitourinary tuberculosis NOS, a condition that is linked to Diabetic Angiopathies. Additionally, the compound is linked to UBA domain containing 1, which also causes Diabetic Angiopathies. These findings suggest that the compound may influence vascular pathways through the regulation of FGF signaling and UBA domain-containing proteins, potentially contributing to the development of diabetic angiopathies. The evidence is supported by multiple scores, indicating a consistent relationship between the compound and the condition, though the exact mechanisms and the compound's role in the pathogenesis remain to be fully elucidated.",
